3\n   <b>\n    Selection Functions\n   </b>\n   choose one value from a set of values.\n        These selection functions are supported:\n  </p>\n  <table class=\"Indent\">\n   <tbody>\n    <tr>\n     <th>\n      Function\n     </th>\n     <th>\n      Explanation\n     </th>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n     <td>\n      <a>\n       MOVE\n      </a>\n     </td>\n     <td>\n      Assign one value to another.\n     </td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n     <td>\n      <a>\n       SEL\n      </a>\n     </td>\n     <td>\n      Returns one of two values depending on a BOOL value.\n     </td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n     <td>\n      <a>\n       MAX\n      </a>\n     </td>\n     <td>\n      Returns the highest value input.\n     </td>\n    </tr>\n   </tbody>\n  </table>\n  <h2>\n   Standards Compliance\n  </h2>\n  <p>\n   IEC 61131-3 Second Edition: Table 27.\n  </p>\n  <p>\n   IEC 61131-3 Third Edition: Table 32.\n  </p>\n  <h2>\n   Further Information\n  </h2>\n  <p>\n   <a>\n    Common Elements\n   </a>\n  </p>\n  <p class=\"Indent\">\n   To learn about other common language elements.\n  </p>\n  <p>\n   <a>\n    Glossary\n   </a>\n  </p>\n  <p class=\"Indent\">\n   For the meaning of terms used in\n   <b>\n    Fernhill\n    <abbr title=\"Supervisory Control and Data Acquisition\">\n     SCADA\n    </abbr>\n   </b>\n   .\n  </p>\n  <p class=\"Footer\">\n   Fernhill SCADA Version 4.0 (20231031.2).  Copyright &copy; 2012-2023 Fernhill Software Ltd: All rights reserved.\n  </p>\n </body>\n</html>\n",
